/F2 11 Tf
50 470 Td
(Key Challenges in Modern Systems:) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Speed Divergence: CPU frequency scales faster than DRAM latency.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Cost Constraint: Fast memory \(SRAM\) is costly; large memory \(DRAM\) is slower.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Capacity Demands: Modern workloads require gigabytes of address space.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- The Ideal Memory: As fast as SRAM, as large as disk, as cheap as flash.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(- Solution: Layered hierarchy leveraging caching and spatial/temporal locality.) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F2 9 Tf
0 -40 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- DLCO Seminar Portal) Tj
ET

