(3. Locality of Reference Principle) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
0 -25 Td
(The Foundation of Caching Effectiveness) Tj
ET
50 500 m 750 500 l S
BT
/F2 11 Tf
50 470 Td
(Temporal Locality \(Locality in Time\):) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  - If a memory location is accessed, it will be accessed again soon.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  - Examples: Loop counters, recurrent variables, subroutines.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(Spatial Locality \(Locality in Space\):) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  - If a location is referenced, adjacent locations are likely to be accessed.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  - Examples: Sequential instruction fetch, array iterations, struct records.) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(Empirical Law: 90/10 Rule - 90% of execution time is spent in 10% of the code.) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F2 9 Tf
0 -40 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- DLCO Seminar Portal) Tj
ET

