/F1 20 Tf
50 540 Td
(4. Effective Memory Access Time \(EMAT\)) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Formula & Numerical Analysis) Tj
ET
50 500 m 750 500 l S
BT
/F2 11 Tf
50 470 Td
(Basic Two-Tier Formula:) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  EMAT = h * Tc + \(1 - h\) * \(Tc + Tm\)) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  Where: h = Hit Ratio, Tc = Cache Access Time, Tm = Main Memory Time) Tj
0 -18 Td
() Tj
0 -18 Td
(Numerical Demonstration:) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  Given Tc = 2 ns, Tm = 50 ns) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  If h = 0.90 \(90% hit rate\):) Tj
0 -18 Td
(    EMAT = 0.90 * 2 + 0.10 * 52 = 1.8 + 5.2 = 7.0 ns) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  If h = 0.98 \(98% hit rate\):) Tj
0 -18 Td
(    EMAT = 0.98 * 2 + 0.02 * 52 = 1.96 + 1.04 = 3.0 ns) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  Conclusion: An 8% hit rate increase more than doubles performance!) Tj
0 -18 Td
/F2 9 Tf
0 -40 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- DLCO Seminar Portal) Tj
ET

